description:
As an IT Internal Audit Manager, your main responsibilities will include:
* Lead and develop Group-wide IT Internal Audit initiatives
* Design, Implement and develop the IT Audit practice at Group level;
* Support Department Head in planning and implementation of the Annual IT Internal Audit Plan;
* Lead the planning and execution of IT internal audit engagements/ Own end-to-end IT audit engagements from planning through reporting.
* Execute IT audit projects within budgeted time and best practices;
* Review IT audit projects working papers, ensuring completeness and assertiveness of conclusions and propose control recommendations to mitigate risks;
* Review audit findings and provide practical risk mitigation and control recommendations.
* Prepare audit reports for assurance and consulting engagements and hold audit Exit Meetings with key audit stakeholders and Management;
* Present audit results and engage with senior stakeholders and management teams.
* Follow up on action plans implementation and remediation of audit findings, prepare status update progress report and perform retesting as required;
* Monitor remediation actions and ensure audit findings are effectively resolved.
* Advanced command of IT environment and IT governance and controls, namely Cybersecurity and AI related;
* Support Process Audit teams in specific ITGC related audit procedures;
